export const SECURITY: Readonly<Record<string, BankSecurity>> = JSON.parse("{\"us-chase\":{\"source\":\"Chase Deposit Account Agreement (chase.com/.../deposit-account-agreement.pdf); Additional Banking Services and Fees for Personal Accounts (ABSF-en.pdf); chase.com/digital/replace-card; chase.com Security Center 'How we protect you'; chase.com education pages on lost credit cards, expired debit cards and card shipping times; Chase Freedom Unlimited Cardmember Agreement (CFPB database), Deposit Account Agreement and fee schedule effective 6/14/2026; card agreement copyright 2019; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"rushFee\":1500,\"rushDays\":2,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Chase refuses to authorize any transaction once a card is reported lost or stolen, and sends a replacement card with a new number; for a credit card the account itself stays open and keeps its age for credit reporting.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Chase monitors cards around the clock and may contact the customer by text message, push notification, email or phone call to confirm whether unusual activity was authorized; fraud alerts are automatic and need no enrollment. Chase can refuse to authorize a transaction it reasonably believes may be fraudulent, but doesn’t say it holds a payment pending the customer's reply.\"},\"us-bank-of-america\":{\"source\":\"Personal Schedule of Fees (bankofamerica.com, rush replacement debit card fee $15.00 per card, waived for Preferred Plus/Honors/Premier and for fraud events); bankofamerica.com/deposits/debit-card-faqs ('There is no fee to replace a debit card', 4-6 business days, lock/unlock); bankofamerica.com/credit-cards/credit-card-security-faq; Deposit Agreement and Disclosures ('If you or we suspect that your account is or may be compromised, we may recommend that you close your account and open a new account'); web.bankofamerica.com/en/security/fraud-protection; Customized Cash Rewards card agreement (fee list has no replacement fee), Schedule of Fees effective 2026-08-07; Deposit Agreement effective 2026-05-15; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"rushFee\":1500,\"standardDays\":6,\"lockInApp\":true,\"newNumberOnFraud\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"For a lost or stolen credit card, the bank says it will cancel the card and send a replacement right away. A debit card can be locked in Online Banking or the app while you look for it, and replaced there or by phone.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The bank watches account activity and sends automatic fraud alerts through the mobile app, text, email or phone. It says it will never ask for personal or financial information by text.\"},\"us-wells-fargo\":{\"source\":\"wellsfargo.com/help/lost-wallet ('as little as 24 hours (additional fees may apply)', 5-7 calendar days, new number); wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings/debit-card-faqs; wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings/debit-card-alerts-faqs; Deposit Account Agreement (merchants 'may receive updated card information'; refusing authorization on suspected fraud); Consumer Account Fee and Information Schedule (no card replacement fee listed); Active Cash Credit Card Account Agreement (Rush Plastic Fee named, no amount; network update services), Fee Schedule and Deposit Account Agreement effective 2026-07-28; credit card pricing as of 2026-06-23; read 2026-09-26\",\"rushDays\":1,\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"A lost or stolen debit or credit card is replaced with a new card number, expiration date and three-digit security code, arriving in about 5 to 7 calendar days. While you look for a misplaced card you can turn it off in the app or online, and recurring charges can still go through.\",\"suspectWords\":\"If it sees unusual card activity, the bank may contact you by phone, email or text asking you to verify the transactions, and it may refuse to authorize a transaction it suspects is fraudulent. Its texts come from short codes such as 93557.\"},\"us-citi\":{\"source\":\"Consumer Deposit Account Agreement fee chart ('Expedited Domestic Delivery of Replacement Debit Card': Waived at every tier; no replacement fee listed; 'For security reasons, we reserve the right to close your account and transfer the balance to a new account' after lost or stolen checks); citi.com what-to-do-when-you-lose-your-credit-card; cardbenefits.citi.com Fraud Early Warning and Credit & Account Protection (Quick Lock); Citi Card Agreement Guide CMA_PID408 (complete fee list, no replacement fee; cardholder must tell merchants when number or expiry changes), Consumer Deposit Account Agreement effective 2025-11-20; read 2026-09-26\",\"rushFee\":0,\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"newNumberOnFraud\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"A replaced credit card comes with a different number, security code and expiration date, usually within about 5 business days. Citi Quick Lock in the app or online blocks new charges on a misplaced card while letting recurring charges continue.\",\"suspectWords\":\"If Citi notices suspicious activity it contacts you by text, email, phone or mail to confirm the activity. Its fraud texts come from short code 95686.\"},\"us-capital-one\":{\"source\":\"capitalone.com/bank/debit-card/activate-my-card ('We'll replace your debit card for free if it's lost, damaged or stolen', 5-7 business days); help-center/checking-savings/getting-your-new-card (Expedited Delivery by FedEx Priority Overnight, 2-3 business days, no fee stated); help-center/fraud-disputes/replacement-card-support (damaged card replaced 'free of charge'); help-center/credit-cards/lost-or-stolen-credit-card; help-center/fraud-disputes/report-fraud; learn-grow credit-card-security-features; help-center/credit-cards/recurring-transactions ('some merchants may automatically update'); Rules Governing Deposit Accounts ('Bank reserves the right to close an Account and assign and transfer the Account information to a replacement Account number ... including when the Account is reported compromised'), Rules Governing Deposit Accounts effective 2026-09-16; 360 Checking disclosures 2026-05-20; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"rushDays\":3,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"newNumberOnFraud\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"When a credit card is reported lost or stolen, Capital One locks it and issues a replacement with a new card number, arriving in about 4 to 6 business days; a lost debit card is deactivated immediately. Eligible customers can use a virtual card in the app while they wait.\",\"suspectWords\":\"If Capital One sees possibly suspicious activity it sends a text, always from the same number, and you can reply on the spot; answering no blocks the card. Alerts also come by email and in the app.\"},\"ca-rbc\":{\"source\":\"rbcroyalbank.com/banking-services/additional-account-services.html; rbcroyalbank.com/banking-services/debit-card.html; rbcroyalbank.com/credit-cards/cardholders/lost-or-stolen-credit-card.html; rbcroyalbank.com/credit-cards/cardholders/frequently-asked-questions/protecting-my-card.html; RBC Royal Bank Credit Card Agreement 15912 (08/2026); rbc.com/sms/en/, Credit Card Agreement 08/2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"RBC cancels a lost or stolen debit card and issues a new one, and blocks a lost or stolen credit card from further use and issues a new card. The first debit card replacement in a calendar year is free and each further one costs $5.00, unless the replacement is due to fraud, a name change, or a card that arrived damaged.\",\"suspectWords\":\"RBC texts the credit cardholder from short code 722373 or 347722 asking them to reply Y to confirm a transaction or N if they don't recognize it, after which a fraud specialist contacts them. The card agreement says RBC can block the card without telling the customer when it suspects fraudulent use.\"},\"ca-td\":{\"source\":\"td.com Access Agreement 804546 (0826); TD Canada Trust List of Services & Fees (effective 2026-03-05); TD Cardholder Agreement 599186 (0326); td.com/ca/en/personal-banking/products/bank-accounts/fraud-claims; td.com/ca/en/personal-banking/advice/day-to-day-banking/fraud-alerts; td.com/ca/en/personal-banking/day-to-day-banking/manage-your-debit-card; td.com/ca/en/personal-banking/advice/day-to-day-banking/lost-stolen-damaged-credit-card, Access Agreement 08/2026; Cardholder Agreement 03/2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"TD closes a lost, stolen or compromised Access Card permanently and issues a replacement that arrives by Canada Post in 5 to 7 business days, or can be picked up the same day at a branch. The customer can lock the card instantly in the TD app while looking for it.\",\"suspectWords\":\"TD texts the credit cardholder when it detects suspicious activity and blocks the card; replying Y unblocks it immediately, while replying N or not answering keeps it blocked until the customer calls, and TD phones if there’s no reply. TD's published fraud alerts cover credit cards; the page doesn’t mention debit cards.\"},\"ca-scotiabank\":{\"source\":\"scotiabank.com/ca/en/personal/credit-cards/fees.html (Fast Card fee $20.00); scotiabank.com digital-banking-guide cardcontrols.html; scotiabank.com digital-banking-guide scotia-fraud-alerts.html; help.scotiabank.com how-can-i-get-a-replacement-credit-card; Day-to-Day Banking Companion Booklet (ScotiaCard Cardholder Agreement); Scotia Momentum Mastercard Cardholder Agreement, credit card fees page current as of 2026-02-01; others read 2026-09-26\",\"rushFee\":2000,\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"A lost or stolen ScotiaCard debit card is reported and replaced in the Scotia app, with the new card arriving in 5 to 10 business days; a lost credit card is reported by phone and the replacement arrives in about 7 to 10 business days. A locked debit card still lets pre-authorized payments and bills set up on it go through.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Scotia Fraud Alerts block the card as soon as an unusual transaction is flagged and contact the customer by app push notification, text from 267373, email, or an automated call. The customer answers Yes or No, and after confirming must try the purchase again.\"},\"ca-bmo\":{\"source\":\"bmo.com/en-ca/main/personal/ways-to-bank/request-replacement-card/; bmo.com/main/personal/ways-to-bank/bmo-debit-mastercard/; bmo.com/main/personal/credit-cards/report-lost-stolen-card/; BMO Credit Card Cardholder Agreement 50463589 (04/25); Agreements, Bank Plans and Fees for Everyday Banking (effective 2026-06-02), Everyday Banking agreements 2026-06-02; Cardholder Agreement 04/2025; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"standardDays\":8,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"BMO lets the customer report a lost or stolen debit or credit card and request a new one online or in the app, and a replacement credit card comes by regular mail in six to eight business days. A misplaced card can be locked online to pause transactions and unlocked later.\",\"suspectWords\":\"BMO's credit card agreement says it may block the card, or a type of transaction, without telling the customer when it suspects unauthorized or fraudulent use. BMO's Canadian pages didn’t describe how a suspected-fraud alert reaches the customer.\"},\"ca-cibc\":{\"source\":\"cibc.com how-to-replace-lost-stolen-card tutorial; cibc.com/en/personal-banking/credit-cards/articles/stolen-credit-card-tips.html; cibc.intelliresponse.com debit lost or stolen answer; cibc.com/en/privacy-security/fraud-alerts.html; CIBC Cardholder Banking Service Agreement 12404-2026/09; CIBC Cardholder Agreement effective 2026-08-01; CIBC debit card brochure 8917; cibc.com additional-service-fees.html, Cardholder Agreement 2026-08-01; Banking Service Agreement 09/2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"CIBC deactivates a lost or stolen credit card immediately and mails a new card with a new number, which can be added to a mobile wallet right away. A lost debit card is protected and replaced once reported at a branch or by phone, and either card can be temporarily locked in online or mobile banking.\",\"suspectWords\":\"CIBC asks the customer to confirm an unusual transaction by text from 242-225 or 242-234 (reply Y or N), by an automated call where they answer on the keypad, or by email. The fraud alerts page doesn’t say whether the card is held until the customer answers.\"},\"mx-bbva\":{\"source\":\"bbva.mx Tarifas y comisiones (Tarifario.pdf, V.229); Ficha Libreton Basico Cuenta Digital (TCR_LibretonBasico_V6.pdf); bbva.mx Tarjeta Azul page; bbva.mx Antifraude help page; bbva.mx 'Bloquea tus tarjetas bancarias desde banca digital'; bbva.mx 'Te robaron o perdiste tu tarjeta de credito' (says to update subscriptions yourself), Tarifario last updated August 2026; Libreton ficha issued 2023-05-23; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":16950,\"replaceFeeCredit\":19200,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The card is blocked from the BBVA app (Emergencies, Theft and loss) or by calling Linea BBVA, and a replacement is requested in the app or at a branch; the new card arrives with a different number and must be activated, and an account holder can keep paying with the digital card meanwhile. Fees exclude 16% IVA: 169.50 pesos for a lost or stolen Libreton Basico debit card (free for damage or renewal) and 192 pesos for the Azul credit card.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When BBVA detects an unusual purchase it sends a push notification through the BBVA app and turns the card off as a precaution, so new purchases are declined; confirming the purchase in the app turns the card back on automatically, and rejecting it leaves the card off and starts a fraud report.\"},\"mx-santander\":{\"source\":\"Santander Cuenta Debito LikeU brochure and fee clause (assets.santandermedia.com); Folleto Informativo Tarjeta de Credito LikeU (MDP_Folleto_LikeU_Dic2025_CAT2026_V4); santander.com.mx help page 'Bloqueo y reposicion de tarjeta' read via Wayback Machine snapshot of 2026-06-10 (live site returned 403), LikeU credit brochure Dec 2025 (CAT calculated 2026-01-01); help page snapshot 2026-06-10; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":7500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":19900,\"rushFee\":10000,\"rushDays\":0,\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer blocks the card in the Santander app (Block and replacement), picks a reason, and then orders a replacement for pickup at a branch: a personalized card is ready at the home branch in 3 to 5 business days, or an unpersonalized card is handed over immediately at any branch. There’s no charge if the card was swallowed by an ATM or the customer was a fraud victim; fees exclude 16% IVA.\"},\"mx-banamex\":{\"source\":\"Banamex Productos de Captacion fee brochure (MiCuenta, OR-V-3148_PE); Cuenta Perfiles fee brochure; banamex.com Tarjeta Clasica tarifas-comisiones; banamex.com App Banamex 'Administracion de tarjetas y cuentas' help; banamex.com 'Necesito bloquear mi tarjeta'; banamex.com Centro de seguridad, MiCuenta brochure 2025-03-03; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":12500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":13000,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer reports the card in the Banamex app (swipe the card, Report) or by phone; the card is canceled and a replacement is generated and sent to the registered address, or it can be collected at a branch by calling 55 1226 2639. Fees exclude IVA: 125 pesos for a MiCuenta or Perfiles debit card and 130 pesos for the Clasica credit card.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Banamex says it will contact the customer if it detects suspicious movement on cards or online banking, and warns it will never ask for a PIN, passwords or SMS codes; it doesn’t say on the pages read whether the purchase is held until confirmed.\"},\"mx-banorte\":{\"source\":\"Folleto Informativo Cuenta Enlace Personal (banorte.com, read via Wayback Machine snapshot of 2026-03-21); Folleto Informativo Tarjeta de Credito Clasica FI-Clasica.pdf (banorte.com, read via Wayback Machine snapshot of 2026-05-15). Live banorte.com timed out on every request., Clasica brochure valid January to June 2026; Enlace Personal brochure undated (its GAT figure is valid to October 2019, so the fee table may be old); read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":12500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":17000,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer reports the lost or stolen card to Banorte; Blindaje Banorte covers fraudulent charges made up to 48 hours before the report on the Clasica credit card at no cost. Fees exclude IVA: 125 pesos to replace a Cuenta Enlace Personal debit card and 170 pesos for the Clasica credit card.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Banorte Avisa sends free SMS notifications meant to protect against unrecognized charges; the brochure doesn’t say whether a suspicious purchase is held until the customer confirms it.\"},\"gb-barclays\":{\"source\":\"barclays.co.uk/help/cards/debit-card/lost-stolen-damaged; barclays.co.uk/help/security-fraud/lost-stolen-card; barclays.co.uk/help/cards/debit-card/replacement-debit-card-arrival; barclays.co.uk/help/accounts/account-services/instant-card-branches; Barclays tariff for personal customers (June 2025) PDF; barclays.co.uk/help/security-fraud/confirm-transaction-text; barclaycard.co.uk/personal/help/fraud-security/lost-or-stolen; barclaycard.co.uk/personal/help/credit-cards/amazon-barclaycard-lost-stolen; barclays.co.uk/help/payments/payment-information/recurring-card-payments.app, tariff correct at 1 June 2025; help pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceWords\":\"The June 2025 tariff has no fee for a standard replacement debit card. Its only card-replacement charge is £12 for a temporary card collected from a branch. Lost, stolen and damaged are handled the same way, except that a damaged card keeps working for 28 days or until the new one is used.\",\"rushFee\":1200,\"rushDays\":0,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Barclays cancels the card and posts a replacement within seven working days by second-class Royal Mail (five if ordered through Online Banking). For an emergency, some branches issue a temporary debit card on the spot for £12, valid for 28 days and limited to two a year. The Barclaycard credit card is blocked permanently from the app and replaced within seven working days. Barclays says it tries to update the new card details with retailers that hold recurring payments on the old debit card (Visa informs most major retailers); others must be told by the customer.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Barclays texts a fraud alert about a suspicious transaction and asks for a Y or N reply, or makes an automated call. It says it may delay or decline an unusual payment, or block the account, until it confirms the customer made it.\"},\"gb-lloyds\":{\"source\":\"lloydsbank.com/help-guidance/everyday-banking/card-and-pin-services/lost-or-stolen-cards (archived 2026-09-22); .../replacement-card (archived 2026-09-24); .../card-freezes (archived 2026-09-10); lloydsbank.com/current-accounts/help-and-guidance/debit-cards (archived 2026-09-17); lloydsbank.com/help-guidance/legal-information/rates-and-charges/services (archived 2026-05-13); lloydsbank.com/credit-cards/help-and-guidance/credit-card-fees (archived 2026-05-09), Wayback snapshots 2026-05 to 2026-09; the live site blocked automated reads; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceWords\":\"The Lloyds service-charges page lists no card replacement fee, and the credit card fees page lists none among its common fees. Neither page says outright that replacement is free.\",\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Lloyds cancels the card straight away, and the cancelation can't be reversed. A new card arrives in five working days. The new card's details show in the app the next day for a debit card, and within five days for a credit card, so they can be used online while the card is in the post.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When spending patterns suggest fraud, Lloyds usually has its automated telephone service call the customer to confirm the purchase, with operators available if it wasn't them. The pages don't say whether the payment is held until the customer confirms it.\"},\"gb-natwest\":{\"source\":\"natwest.com/support-centre/help-with-your-card/card-functionality/how-do-i-report-a-lost-stolen-or-damaged-debit-card-and-order-a-replacement; natwest.com/support-centre/payments/general/how-do-i-report-a-lost-stolen-or-damaged-credit-card-and-order-a-replacement; natwest.com/current-accounts/rates-and-charges (Safe custody, travel money and additional services); natwest.com/credit-cards/existing-customers/fees-and-charges; natwest.com/support-centre/help-with-your-card/fraud/i-have-a-message-from-the-fraud-team-what-do-i-do; Your Current Account Terms PDF (changes from 1 October 2026), read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"The current-account additional services charges list \\\"Replacing lost or damaged cards: No Charge\\\". The credit card fee page doesn't mention replacement.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"NatWest cancels the card, and issues a new PIN if the PIN may be compromised. The new card arrives within 10 working days, and its details can be used from the app's See details feature meanwhile. Emergency cash from a cash machine after reporting a card lost or stolen is free. Its current account terms say it may enroll a replacement card in the card scheme's automatic updater, although its help pages still tell customers to update subscriptions themselves.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When NatWest restricts a card over suspected fraud, its fraud team sends texts, automated calls and voicemails, then an email or letter. The block stays on the card until the customer contacts the fraud team.\"},\"gb-hsbc\":{\"source\":\"hsbc.co.uk/help/card-support/lost-or-stolen; hsbc.co.uk/help/card-support/block-unblock; HSBC personal banking terms and conditions and charges PDF (effective 6 July 2026); hsbc.co.uk/current-accounts/interest-rates-and-charges; hsbc.co.uk/credit-cards/fees, terms effective 2026-07-06; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceWords\":\"Neither the HSBC current-account charges page, the credit card fees page nor the personal banking terms (effective 6 July 2026) lists a card replacement fee.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"HSBC cancels the card straight away and posts a new one within 5-7 working days in the UK, or 12 working days abroad. The new card can be added to Apple Pay or Google Pay from the app before it arrives. A found card must not be used without contacting HSBC first.\",\"suspectWords\":\"HSBC's terms say it contacts the customer the quickest secure way, which might be a text or a phone call, when there’s actual or suspected fraud. It may block the card while it suspects fraud, and unblocks it once the reason ends.\"},\"gb-santander\":{\"source\":\"santander.co.uk/personal/support/fraud-and-security/lost-or-stolen-cards; santander.co.uk/personal/support/customer-support/new-cards; santander.co.uk/personal/support/fraud-and-security/how-to-report-fraud; Interest rates and fees for current accounts PDF (BANK0501APR25), fees correct at 28 April 2025; pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceWords\":\"The interest rates and fees document for current accounts (28 April 2025) lists no card replacement fee. Lost, stolen and damaged cards are all reported the same way.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"Santander blocks the old card and sends a new one within 5-7 working days, keeping the same PIN unless a new one is requested. Digital wallets keep working meanwhile, and a branch can give access to cash with ID. The new card has a new number, which doesn't affect Direct Debits or standing orders.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Santander sometimes declines a payment that doesn't look right. It then checks with the customer by an app push notification, a text to the registered mobile (a Y or N reply), or a phone call. Once the customer confirms, the payment can be made again.\"},\"gb-nationwide\":{\"source\":\"nationwide.co.uk/help/payments/lost-stolen-or-damaged-cards; Guide to your Current Account P4471 (January 2026) PDF; nationwide.co.uk/help/fraud-and-security/fraud-alert-messages; nationwide.co.uk/help/fraud-and-security/card-fraud; nationwide.co.uk/current-accounts/help/debit-cards, guide January 2026; pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Nationwide says it replaces broken or damaged cards free of charge. The Guide to your Current Account (January 2026) lists no replacement fee for lost or stolen cards either, but doesn’t say free. A damaged credit card needs a phone call.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"Nationwide cancels the card and issues a new one, and the new card can be used online as soon as it shows in the app. Nationwide says not to freeze a card that’s actually lost or stolen, only a misplaced one. A frozen card still lets recurring card payments, Direct Debits and wallet payments through.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Nationwide blocks the card, then sends a fraud alert by app push notification, two texts, or an automated voice call. There are 2 hours to answer in the app before the alert moves to text. The card stays blocked until the customer replies, and it works again within minutes of confirming.\",\"freeFor\":[\"damaged\"]},\"ie-aib\":{\"source\":\"AIB 'A guide to fees and charges for personal accounts' (PDF); AIB Debit Card Terms and Conditions of Use (PDF, cl. 3.5 card updater); AIB Personal Credit Card T&C (PDF, cond. 29 card updater); aib.ie/Credit-Card-Fees-and-Charges; aib.ie help pages report-lost-stolen-card, order-replacement-aib-card; aib.ie text-alerts-faqs; aib.ie mobile-banking-app-cards (freeze), Fee guide 1 July 2026; debit T&C effective 20 May 2026; credit T&C effective 25 Aug 2025; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"The personal fee guide lists debit card issue and replacement under services with no charge. The credit card fee page lists no replacement fee at all, but it doesn't say one is free either.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You report the card lost or stolen in the app, online banking, a branch kiosk or by phone at any hour; the card is canceled and a new one is posted to your address. A card in Apple Pay or Google Pay updates to the new card on its own: a debit card by 5pm the next working day, a credit card at once.\",\"suspectWords\":\"AIB texts the transaction (amount, merchant, last four digits) and asks you to reply 1 if it's yours or 9 if not; replying 9 places a hold on the card and the cards team contacts you. If you don't reply within 8 hours, a hold is placed on the card and you must phone; the reply to a 1 says to check whether the payment went through, so the payment itself may have been declined.\"},\"ie-bank-of-ireland\":{\"source\":\"Schedule of Fees and Charges for Personal Customers (PDF, Aug-25); personalbanking.bankofireland.com visa-debit/fees and classic-credit-card/fees; bankofireland.com help pages: can-report-lost-stolen-card, long-will-take-receive-replacement-visa-debit-card, can-order-replacement-credit-card, what-is-visa-account-updater-vau; credit-cards/card-controls; bankofireland.com/security-zone, Fee schedule effective 1 Aug 2025; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceWords\":\"The Personal Current Account section of the 2025 fee schedule lists no debit card replacement fee. The only replacement fee in it, EUR 8.00 for a lost, stolen or damaged card, is for the ATM card on a deposit account. The Classic Credit Card fee page lists no replacement fee. A damaged credit card is reissued with the same number, CVV and expiry date.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You phone the 24/7 line; the bank cancels the card as soon as you report it and sends a new one to your address on file in 5 to 7 working days (standardDays is the upper bound). You can be liable for losses up to the moment you report it.\",\"suspectWords\":\"If the bank suspects fraud on a debit or credit card, it may text asking you to confirm the transaction by replying YES or NO. Its pages don't say whether the payment is held until you reply.\"},\"ie-ptsb\":{\"source\":\"PTSB General Terms & Conditions and Personal & Business Banking Charges (PDF bmk2548, via web.archive.org, as ptsb.ie returns 403); ptsb.ie help pages report-my-card-lost-or-stolen, replace-lost-stolen-card, replace-my-damaged-card, manage-cards, card-frozen-what-to-do-next, how-we-keep-you-safe (via web.archive.org), Charges booklet 15 Jan 2025; help pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":500,\"replaceWords\":\"EUR 5.00 each to replace a lost or stolen debit card or credit card. The fee list charges only for lost or stolen cards; a damaged card is replaced through a separate process with no fee listed.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You report it in the app, in Open24 online banking or by phone at any hour; the card is canceled and the new card and PIN arrive separately within 5 to 7 working days (standardDays is the upper bound). A debit card replaced as lost or stolen updates in your digital wallet automatically; one replaced as damaged or expired takes up to 2 business days.\",\"suspectWords\":\"PTSB's fraud monitoring may contact you by phone, text or letter to verify unusual activity; texts only ask for a Yes or No reply or a call to the fraud line, and a No blocks the card. The bank also says it may temporarily block specific card and ATM transactions it considers unusual until you call.\"},\"is-landsbankinn\":{\"source\":\"Verðskrá Landsbankans (price list, PDF) items 2.8.1 and 2.8.6; Almennir viðskiptaskilmálar Landsbankans no. 1532-06 (general terms, ch. 5); landsbankinn.is/einstaklingar/greidslukort; landsbankinn.is/nytt-kort, Price list effective 23 Apr 2026; general terms June 2023; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":190000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":190000,\"replaceWords\":\"ISK 1,900 for a new payment card (debit or credit) to replace a lost or stolen one. No fee is listed for a damaged card.\",\"rushFee\":1450000,\"rushDays\":3,\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You freeze the card in the app straight away, or call 410 4000 (525 2000 outside hours); once reported, the card is closed temporarily or permanently. The new card has a new number but works online as soon as it's created, and the plastic follows in 5 to 10 working days, or 2 to 3 by express delivery (both day counts are the upper bound).\",\"suspectWords\":\"The terms let the bank decline authorization and close a card on reasonable suspicion of fraud, and say the cardholder is notified of the closure, which is reversed if the suspicion proves unfounded. The bank's pages don't say whether it contacts you by text, app or phone.\"},\"is-arion\":{\"source\":\"Verðskrá Arion banka - einstaklingar (PDF) items 12.2.1, 12.3.10, 13.1.2; Kreditkortaskilmálar Arion banka (credit card terms, PDF 18.1.8.22); arionbanki.is/hjalp/glatad-kort-frysta-kort, Price list effective 23 Sep 2026; credit terms in force from 7 May 2019; web page read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":249000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":249000,\"replaceWords\":\"ISK 2,490 to reissue a lost card, for both debit and credit. The credit card terms say a defective card is replaced free.\",\"rushFee\":1350000,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You freeze the card in the app and report it to customer service at 444 7000 (weekdays 9 to 4) or the emergency line at 525 2000; a frozen card can be unfrozen in the app if it turns up. While the card is frozen, subscriptions and phone or watch payments keep working.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The credit card terms say that on reasonable suspicion of fraud the bank may decline authorization and notify the cardholder without delay, and reopens authorization at once if the suspicion proves unfounded. The channel (text, app or phone) isn't stated.\"},\"is-islandsbanki\":{\"source\":\"Verðskrá Íslandsbanka fyrir einstaklinga (PDF) items 1.3 and 4.37; Skilmálar debetkorta EY-9092 (debit terms, PDF); Skilmálar kreditkorta EY-9096 (credit terms, PDF, cl. 7.3, 10.4, 11.8, 14); islandsbanki.is leidbeiningar-stolid-kort; gott-ad-vita-um-kortin, Price list effective 19 Mar 2026; debit terms from 18 Mar 2026; credit terms from 27 Mar 2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":110000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":220000,\"replaceWords\":\"Debit cards cost ISK 1,100 for a new card or renewal, and credit cards ISK 2,200 to reissue. The credit terms charge the reissue fee when a card was lost and not when it was defective, and a defective card is replaced free.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The terms require you to freeze the card in the bank's app at once and report it on 440-4000 (the emergency line is open 24 hours), and the card is then closed. To get a replacement you give a lost-card statement and apply for a new card; a credit card reported temporarily lost can be reopened if the request arrives by the next banking day.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The debit terms say that on reasonable suspicion of fraud the bank may refuse authorizations and close the card, notifying the cardholder without delay afterwards, and reopens it if the suspicion proves unfounded. The channel isn't stated.\"},\"fr-bnp-paribas\":{\"source\":\"BNP Paribas 'Conditions et tarifs, produits et services pour les particuliers' (MoneyVox archive copy); mabanque.bnpparibas opposition-carte-bancaire page; mabanque.bnpparibas carte-virtuelle page; mabanque.bnpparibas security-alerts pages (search excerpts), tariff effective 1 January 2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":1500,\"replaceWords\":\"Tariff line is 'reissuing a card before expiry': 15 EUR, free for Visa Premier, Visa Infinite and virtual cards and for BNP Paribas Sécurité insurance holders. Stopping (blocking) the card is free. No separate standard credit card: the credit figure is the deferred-debit Visa Classic, which falls under the same line.\",\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Reporting the card lost or stolen (by app, website, the 3477 line or a branch) takes effect immediately, is free and can't be undone; it has to be confirmed in writing. Unless told otherwise, BNP orders a new card automatically, with a new card number and a new PIN, which takes 5 business days, and a virtual card is available right away.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When BNP spots suspicious activity it sends a text asking you to call its 3477 line; it says its advisors will never phone you about fraud. It doesn’t say whether the payment is held until you confirm.\"},\"fr-societe-generale\":{\"source\":\"SG 'Conditions appliquées aux opérations bancaires – Particuliers' brochure (static.sg.fr sg-bt-2026.pdf); particuliers.sg.fr faire-opposition-carte-bancaire; particuliers.sg.fr selfcare page; particuliers.sg.fr verrouillage-temporaire-carte-bancaire; particuliers.sg.fr vishing (search excerpt), tariff effective 1 April 2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":2000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":2000,\"replaceWords\":\"20 EUR per card for damage or an early reissue, and 20 EUR after stopping a card for loss, theft or fraud; free on normal renewal or a malfunction, and included in the JAZZ and Sobrio bundles. SG does sell a separate revolving credit card (CB Visa Alterna); the credit figure applies the same card-replacement line to it.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You can stop the card 24/7 in the SG app or online. The block is immediate and permanent, and you're told by text, push or email. A new card is made automatically and sent to your home or branch, with the same PIN unless you ask for a new one. Home delivery is free, except that a card reissued with a new PIN can only be collected at a branch.\",\"suspectWords\":\"SG says it will never call to ask you to cancel, block, validate or confirm a payment, or to read out a code or your card number. If in doubt, hang up and call 3933 yourself. The pages read don't say how SG itself flags a suspicious card payment. Card-detail updates to merchants are an opt-in service that only reaches participating online merchants.\"},\"fr-lcl\":{\"source\":\"LCL 'Guide tarifaire des produits et services – Particuliers, applicable au 1er janvier 2026' (portail-lcl-web.cdn.prismic.io PDF); lcl.fr/questions-frequentes/sos-cartes, tariff effective 1 January 2026; FAQ read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1330,\"replaceFeeCredit\":1330,\"replaceWords\":\"13.30 EUR to replace a card at your request (damage, a new design or an early reissue). The tariff lists no replacement fee after loss or theft, and stopping the card is free. LCL does sell a revolving Visa Crédit Renouvelable card; the credit figure applies the same general line to it.\",\"rushFee\":5850,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You stop the card 24/7 from the LCL Mes Comptes app (the SOS Carte service) or by phone. A virtual card is available in the app right away, until the new physical card arrives. Sending the card by registered mail or Chronopost costs 10 EUR plus postage.\",\"suspectWords\":\"LCL sends fraud alerts by text or email and asks you to call its fraud line (+33 969 391 133). It doesn’t say whether the payment is held. Card-detail updates to merchants are an opt-in, free 'automatic card update' option for online merchants.\",\"freeFor\":[\"lost\",\"stolen\"]},\"fr-credit-agricole\":{\"source\":\"Crédit Agricole d'Ile-de-France 'Principales conditions tarifaires applicables aux particuliers, en vigueur au 01.04.26' (MoneyVox archive, scanned) and April 2025 edition; credit-agricole.fr card product pages (4-year validity); credit-agricole.fr/ca-paris carte-bancaire FAQ; credit-agricole.fr applications/ma-banque; credit-agricole.fr fraud pages, tariff effective 1 April 2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":1000,\"replaceWords\":\"'Early reissue' is 10 EUR in the Île-de-France tariff: the scanned April 2026 grid's value column is misaligned, but the April 2025 grid clearly shows 10 EUR. Stopping a card for loss or theft is free. No standalone price for replacing a lost or stolen card is listed; it’s included in the account bundles. No separate standard credit card: the credit figure is the deferred-debit card under the same line.\",\"cardYears\":4,\"cardYearsCredit\":4,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You stop the card through your branch or the 24/7 line, 09 69 39 92 91, and have to confirm by registered letter to your branch. The advisor orders a new card, and Crédit Agricole's virtual card can be used until it arrives.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Crédit Agricole says it will never ask you to validate or block payments remotely, or for codes received by text. If you suspect fraud, stop the card straight away. The pages read don't describe how the bank flags a suspicious payment. Card-detail updates to merchants are an opt-in setting in the Ma Banque app.\"},\"fr-la-banque-postale\":{\"source\":\"La Banque Postale 'Particuliers – Tarifs au 1er janvier 2026, Conditions et tarifs' (labanquepostale.fr PDF); labanquepostale.fr FAQ comment-faire-opposition-sur-ma-carte, comment-bloquer-temporairement-ma-carte, carte-abimee-ou-defectueuse; labanquepostale.fr alertes-et-fraudes, tariff effective 1 January 2026; web pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":1500,\"replaceWords\":\"Early reissue ('renouvellement anticipé') is 15 EUR, and 15 EUR for a withdrawal-only card. Stopping a card is free. The tariff has no separate line for replacement after loss or theft. No separate standard credit card: the credit figure is the deferred-debit Visa, under the same line.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"You stop the card 24/7 in the app, online or on 3639. It’s blocked at once, you must confirm in writing, and the new card arrives 'within a few days'.\",\"suspectWords\":\"La Banque Postale says it watches transactions for suspicious ones and sends a text when a transaction is accepted or refused. If you didn't make the payment, you contact your advisor straight away. It will never ask for codes received by text.\"},\"de-deutsche-bank\":{\"source\":\"deutsche-bank.de Preis- und Leistungsverzeichnis der Deutsche Bank AG (PDF); FAQ 'Wie sperre ich meine Karten?'; FAQ 'Wie bestelle ich eine Ersatzkarte für meine Debitkarte/SparCard?'; 3D Secure / Sicherheitspaket page; Bedingungen für die Debitkarten (Stand 01/2025); Bedingungen für die Kreditkarten (Stand 06/2021), PLV Stand 23.09.2026\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"PLV 'Bestellung einer Ersatzkarte' lists Deutsche Bank Card (girocard debit; Card Plus is a Debit Mastercard) and Mastercard/Visa credit cards (all versions) as free of charge, with no distinction by loss, theft, damage or fault.\",\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer blocks the card in online banking or the app (Services > Card > block and/or replace) or by calling the 24/7 card line (069 910-10035); a replacement can be ordered in the same step. Only a block-and-replace flow is described; no self-service temporary freeze was found.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When a card transaction looks unusual, the bank immediately sends a text to the stored mobile number and the customer replies by text to say whether they made the payment. Whether the payment is held until confirmed isn’t stated.\"},\"de-commerzbank\":{\"source\":\"commerzbank.de Preis- und Leistungsverzeichnis (PDF); FAQs 'Wie bestelle ich eine neue Girocard?', 'Ich habe meine Karte verloren - wie sperre ich meine Girocard?', 'Wie sperre ich eine Kreditkarte bei Verlust/Diebstahl?', 'Wie sperre ich eine Kreditkarte temporär?', 'Wie bestelle ich eine Ersatzkreditkarte?', 'Verwendung einer neuen Girocard', PLV Stand 01.09.2026\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1500,\"replaceWords\":\"Girocard (with Visa debit function) replacement costs 15.00 EUR, charged when the customer asks for it because of a name change, a customer-initiated account switch, or a lost, stolen or misused card, unless the bank is responsible for the cause. The FAQ says a replacement for a defect is 15.00 EUR and loss/theft 'may' be free. The PLV lists no replacement fee for credit cards.\",\"cardYears\":4,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer blocks the card in the banking app or online banking ('Karte sperren') or by phone (24/7 card-block line +49 69 5050 2040 for credit cards); a lost or stolen credit card is automatically replaced with a new card and PIN by post, and the card number and PIN change (a defect replacement keeps both). A self-set temporary block on a credit card, and a girocard block, can be lifted again in the app or online banking.\"},\"de-postbank\":{\"source\":\"postbank.de Postbank-Preis-und-Leistungsverzeichnis-923-959-000-0726.pdf; Bedingungen für die Debitkarten 923 933 018 01.25; 'Karten vermisst – das müssen Sie tun'; 'Karte sperren und Ersatzkarte bestellen', PLV Stand 01.07.2026\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"The PLV (Stand 1 July 2026) has no replacement-card line at all; Postbank's 'Karten vermisst' page states blocking and the replacement card cost 0.00 EUR. The debit card terms allow a PLV fee for loss/theft/misuse replacements only if the bank isn’t responsible, but no such fee is listed. Debit card is the Postbank Card (girocard with Debit Mastercard function); credit card is the Postbank Mastercard (29 EUR/yr).\",\"lostCardWords\":\"The debit card can be blocked by the customer in online banking or the app, or by phone (0228 5500 5500); a credit card is blocked by phone (0228 5500 5525, 24/7). A replacement card arrives automatically by post within a few days, with a new PIN mailed separately after loss or theft (a defect replacement keeps the old PIN). No self-service temporary freeze was found.\"},\"de-ing\":{\"source\":\"ing.de/preis-leistungsverzeichnis (Stand 26.09.2026); ing.de/hilfe/zahlungsverkehr/karten/karte-sperren; ing.de/hilfe/sicherheit; ing.de/wissen/karte-sperren; ing.de/hilfe/zahlungsverkehr/karten/folgekarte, PLV Stand 26.09.2026\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1000,\"replaceWords\":\"PLV: replacement card 10 EUR (VISA Card debit and girocard), payable only if the customer is responsible for the cause (loss, theft, misuse, defect, name change). ING's help page table: theft/loss/misuse free, defect 10 EUR, expiry free, name change or new card on request 10 EUR. ING issues no standard credit card; its 'VISA Card' is a debit card.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer blocks the card in the ING app or online banking, or via 116 116 or 069 / 34 22 24; a permanent block can’t be undone and a new card with a new card number is sent automatically by post within a few days. A temporary block (VISA Card only) takes effect at once and the customer can lift it themselves.\"},\"de-berliner-sparkasse\":{\"source\":\"berliner-sparkasse.de Preis- und Leistungsverzeichnis (15.07.2026); Bedingungen für die Sparkassen-Card (Fassung Juli 2026); Bedingungen für die Mastercard/Visa Card (Kreditkarte) (Fassung März 2026); Card Control page; Kartenverlust page, PLV Stand 15.07.2026\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Sparkassen-Card (girocard debit) and Mastercard/Visa credit card: replacement for a lost, stolen or misused card 0.00 EUR; for a name change 0.00 EUR; for a damaged card 15.00 EUR only where the customer is responsible for the damage.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer calls 116 116 or the bank's 24/7 lines (Sparkassen-Card 030 869 869 05, credit card 030 245 524 00) or blocks online; blocking is free, and police should be told of a theft (the only way to stop direct-debit (ELV) use of the card). Whether a replacement is sent automatically wasn’t confirmed on a page read; the app's Card Control only switches card functions off temporarily and isn’t a full block.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Card Control sends a real-time push or email alert when someone tries to use a card function the customer has switched off; no bank-initiated fraud call or text process was found.\"},\"es-santander\":{\"source\":\"wcm.bancosantander.es/fwm/do-o-8-2-0-precios_estandar.pdf (Epígrafe 5 Tarjetas, items 10, 18, 22, Nota 10); bancosantander.es/faqs/particulares/tarjetas/desbloquear-tarjeta-de-credito-debito/; bancosantander.es/faqs/particulares/tarjetas/que-hacer-robo-perdida-tarjeta-credito/; bancosantander.es/faqs/particulares/tarjetas/solicitar-renovacion-duplicado-tarjeta/, Card tariff section in force since 2023-07-11; FAQs read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":500,\"replaceWords\":\"Tariff item 10: €5.00 per duplicate card, charged only when the cause of the reissue is attributable to the customer (so no loss/theft/damage split is published). The same tariff also has a separate line for a duplicate physical card (its figure could not be matched to its row with confidence) and €3.00 for delivery to the home on request.\",\"rushFee\":7000,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"A card blocked permanently for loss or theft can’t be reactivated, and Santander automatically generates a replacement card. If the card may only be mislaid, the customer can switch it off temporarily in the app or online banking and switch it back on when it turns up, which avoids waiting for a new card.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Not found on Santander Spain's own pages. The tariff lists an optional paid SMS alert service that texts the customer about every card transaction so they can spot fraud and block the card themselves; no bank-initiated confirm-or-decline process is described.\",\"freeFor\":[\"stolen\"]},\"es-bbva\":{\"source\":\"BBVA Libro de tarifas Epígrafe 17 Tarjetas (bbva.es epigrafe-17-tarjetas-credito-debito-prepago.pdf, via web.archive.org 2024-06-22); bbva.es/general/ayuda-urgente.html (archived 2026-08-12); bbva.es/general/seguridad/herramientas/apagar-tarjetas.html (archived 2026-06-09); bbva.es/finanzas-vistazo/ciberseguridad/ultima-hora/resolvemos-tus-dudas-sobre-medios-de-pago-cuentas-y-transacciones.html, Tariff in force since 2024-02-15; help pages read 2026-09-26 (bbva.es blocks direct fetch, read via Wayback)\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":400,\"replaceFeeCredit\":600,\"replaceWords\":\"€4.00 for a debit-card duplicate and €6.00 for a credit-card duplicate; under note 6, the fee is charged only when the cause of the reissue is attributable to the customer. No separate loss/theft/damage figures.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Blocking the card (in the app, on bbva.es or by phone) automatically sends a new card under the same contract that keeps the PIN but has a new card number, so the old card's transaction history doesn't carry over. If the customer only limits or switches the card off instead, they can switch the same card back on without needing a new one.\",\"suspectWords\":\"No bank-initiated fraud call or text procedure found on BBVA Spain pages. If someone tries to use a switched-off card, the customer gets a notification that it must be switched back on. Customers can set up personal alerts in the app or on the web, and they report unrecognized transactions themselves by app, web, ATM or phone.\",\"freeFor\":[\"stolen\"]},\"es-caixabank\":{\"source\":\"caixabank.es 2100e07d.pdf Epígrafe 7 Servicios de pago (D - Otros servicios); caixabank.es/particular/cards/faqs-about-bank-cards.html; caixabank.es/particular/tarjetas-bancarias/todo-lo-que-debes-saber-para-anular-una-tarjeta-extraviada-o-robada-p.html; caixabank.com press release 'CaixaBank amplía de cinco a siete años el plazo de validez de todas sus tarjetas', Tariff in force since 2022-07-08 (latest found); validity press release 2023-08-23; FAQs read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":500,\"replaceWords\":\"The payment-services tariff lists 'Duplicado de tarjeta' at €5.00 per duplicate, with no split by card type or by loss, theft or damage. The English FAQ says the price of an urgent or international replacement is quoted when the card is requested, and in Spain a branch can hand over a replacement card on the spot.\",\"cardYears\":7,\"cardYearsCredit\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer blocks the card in CaixaBankNow or CaixaBank Pay (temporarily or permanently) or by phone, and can order the duplicate in the same step. In Spain they can also go to a branch to get a card immediately or turn on mobile payments.\",\"suspectWords\":\"CaixaBank says it sends fraud alerts and card-block notices by SMS and/or push notification through the CaixaBankNow app when the customer needs to know at once. A decline-until-confirmed process isn’t described.\"},\"es-sabadell\":{\"source\":\"Banco Sabadell Epígrafe 90 (assets.bancsabadell.com serivios_pagos_tarifa_caspdf), sections 3.2 and 3.7; bancsabadell.com Protección de tarjetas page; blog.bancsabadell.com 2023/07 pagos-digitales-viaja-tranquilo (archived 2025-05-16), Tariff in force since 2026-04-10; pages read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":301,\"replaceFeeCredit\":301,\"replaceWords\":\"€3.01 per replacement card when the cause is attributable to the cardholder (section 3.7, applying to cardholders generally). There’s no loss/theft/damage split. Delivery to the home on request is an extra €3.01.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"In the app (My Card > Turn off, block or replace), the customer can switch a missing card off temporarily and back on, or block it permanently after loss or theft and ask for a replacement. Sabadell's free card-protection service refunds fraudulent transactions made in the 48 hours before the loss or theft was reported.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Sabadell's free card-protection service texts the customer about every credit or debit card transaction over €150, and the customer must phone the bank at once if they didn't make it. A decline-until-confirmed process wasn’t found on Sabadell's own pages.\"},\"es-bankinter\":{\"source\":\"docs.bankinter.com ine_tarjeta_visa_clasica_bankinter_.pdf (INE Visa Clásica); empresas.bankinter.com Epígrafe 9 0128e09d.pdf (via Wayback, in force 2012-06-11); bankinter.com/blog/noticias-bankinter/duplicado-tarjeta-bankinter (2021-02-23, via Wayback); bankinter.com/blog/noticias-bankinter/tarjeta-credito-perdida (archived 2025-12-02); bankinter.com/banca/en/faqs/accounts/what-cards-are-associated-with-the-payroll-account-how-many-days-does-it-take (archived 2025-04-19), INE undated; blog 2021-02-23; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeCredit\":2500,\"replaceWords\":\"The pre-contract information for the Visa Clásica credit card charges €25 per duplicate or second card. An older 2012 card tariff (Epígrafe 9) listed €3.00 for a duplicate when the cause is attributable to the customer. No current debit-card duplicate fee was found.\",\"standardDays\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Requesting a duplicate blocks the current card immediately, and a new card arrives inactive by ordinary mail at the home address within 5 days (5 business days for a new account's card; it can be collected at a branch to save time). For a card that may just be lost, the customer can switch it off temporarily in the app or on the web and switch it back on, or block it permanently.\"},\"jp-mufg\":{\"source\":\"bk.mufg.jp/tsukau/tetsuduki/card/loss/index.html; faq01.bk.mufg.jp/faq/show/603; bk.mufg.jp/column/cashless/b006.html; faq.cr.mufg.jp/mufgcard/detail?id=329; cr.mufg.jp/member/new/20110104_01.html; cr.mufg.jp/carduse/misappropriate/procedure/index.html, read 2026-09-26 (credit reissue fee from 2011-01-04 notice)\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":55000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":100000,\"replaceWords\":\"Cash card or MUFG Debit reissue after loss or theft costs 550 yen (tax included) through the app, 1,100 yen by phone or at a branch. MUFG Card (credit) reissue was set at 1,000 yen before consumption tax in a 2011 notice (no current tax-included figure found); Gold and Platinum reissue free. Cash card delivery is stated as about 1 week to 10 days, so standardDays = 8 business days.\",\"standardDays\":8,\"cardYears\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer reports the loss in the MUFG app (24/7 immediate suspension) or by phone to the loss center, and the card is stopped at once; reissue can be requested in the same step and the new card comes by registered mail that isn’t forwarded. A reissued debit card carries a new card number.\",\"suspectWords\":\"For the MUFG Card, when a suspicious charge is detected the transaction is held and the cardholder is asked to confirm by email, SMS, an automated call or an operator call; if they deny it, the card is replaced with a new number. The debit card sends a usage notice email for each purchase.\"},\"jp-smbc\":{\"source\":\"smbc.co.jp/kojin/otetsuduki/saihakko/card/; smbc.co.jp/kojin/olive-account/regulation/pdf/flexible-pay-manual.pdf; smbc-card.com/mem/goriyo/notes.jsp; smbc-card.com/mem/goriyo/lost.jsp; smbc-card.com/mem/service/sec/system.jsp (search excerpt), read 2026-09-26 (Olive manual version 2024-05-28)\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":110000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Cash card reissue is 1,100 yen (tax included); Olive Flexible Pay is free except at the Olive Standard rank, which pays 1,100 yen on loss or theft. Sumitomo Mitsui Card (credit) reissue is free when done online and 1,100 yen by phone (Gold and above free). Bank cards arrive in 1-2 weeks, so standardDays = 10 business days; credit cards in about 1 week to 10 days.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The cardholder reports online or by phone; the card company either stops the card permanently and reissues it with a new number, or places a temporary restriction that can be lifted if the card turns up. Reissued credit and debit cards always get a new card number.\",\"suspectWords\":\"A 24/7 fraud detection system restricts the card when a charge looks like fraud and contacts the cardholder by email, phone or SMS; answering through the link in the notice that the charge was theirs reopens the card.\"},\"jp-mizuho\":{\"source\":\"mizuhobank.co.jp/tetsuduki/card_saihakko/index.html (via web.archive.org capture 2025-12-21, page dated 2024-11-10); faq.mizuhobank.co.jp/faq/show/27; faq.mizuhobank.co.jp/faq/show/21; faq.mizuhobank.co.jp/faq/show/7718; faq.mizuhobank.co.jp/faq/show/12150, page dated 2024-11-10; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":110000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":110000,\"replaceWords\":\"Cash card reissue is 1,100 yen (tax included) for loss or theft and free for a failed chip or stripe or wear damage; the page also lists 550 yen for a switch or reissue, apparently the online (Mizuho Direct) rate. Mileage Club credit card reissue is 1,100 yen depending on the reason. Cash card arrives about 10 days after a branch request, 1-2 weeks online, so standardDays = 10 business days; credit or debit-linked cards take 2-4 weeks.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer calls the branch on weekdays or the 24-hour loss center, and the bank stops transactions immediately and explains how to reissue. A card found after being reported lost can’t be used again until the customer reopens it at a branch.\",\"freeFor\":[\"damaged\"]},\"jp-resona\":{\"source\":\"resonabank.co.jp/kojin/faq/tetsuduki/faq_tetsuduki_0007.html, _0026.html, _0006.html; resonabank.co.jp/kojin/visa_debit/oshirase_c/20220225_visadebit.html; resonabank.co.jp/kojin/gochui/detail/phishing_card.html; resonacard.co.jp/visa/faq/trouble/faq_p_visa_trouble_0001.html (all via web.archive.org captures 2025-01 to 2026-05; live site returns 403), captures 2025-01-27 to 2026-05-15; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":110000,\"replaceWords\":\"Cash card and Resona Debit (Visa) reissue is 1,100 yen (tax included) per card for loss, theft or a forgotten PIN; free for a damaged card. Resona Card (credit) says only that a set reissue fee applies. Mailed cards arrive in 10-14 days, so standardDays = 10 business days; a branch can usually issue the card on the spot, with no separate charge listed beyond the reissue fee.\",\"rushFee\":0,\"rushDays\":0,\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer phones the branch (weekdays) or the after-hours center to stop the card, and can also set the cash card or debit function to suspended and back in the Resona Group app, though a lost card must still be reported to the bank. The replacement is ordered online or at a branch, where it’s normally handed over the same day.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The bank runs 24/7 fraud monitoring on the debit card and asks customers to check their statements and call 0120-24-3989 about any withdrawal they don't recognize; no outbound contact method is described.\",\"freeFor\":[\"damaged\"]},\"jp-japan-post-bank\":{\"source\":\"jp-bank.japanpost.jp/tetuzuki/funsitu/tzk_fst_index.html; faq.jp-bank.japanpost.jp/faq_detail.html?id=10757; ?id=10446; ?id=10456; ?id=1149; ?id=998; jp-bank.japanpost.jp/kojin/cashless/yuchodebit/kj_crd_dbt_security.html, read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":110000,\"replaceWords\":\"Reissuing a card or passbook after loss or theft costs 1,100 yen (tax included) each; Yucho Debit reissue may carry the same 1,100 yen fee. JP BANK Card (credit) reissue may carry a fee, amount not stated (Gold free). A cash card arrives about 2 weeks after the request, so standardDays = 10 business days; a JP BANK credit card takes about one month.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"cardYears\":5,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer calls the 24-hour card loss center or uses a web form, and the bank stops transactions on the card; the replacement is applied for at a Japan Post Bank or post office counter with passbook, seal and ID and is sent by registered mail. A card found afterward stays stopped until the customer lifts the stop in person at a counter.\",\"suspectWords\":\"Yucho Debit is monitored for fraud 24/7 and the bank sends a usage confirmation email to the registered address; customers can switch the debit card off and on themselves on the Yucho Debit member website (the passbook app can’t stop a cash card).\"},\"kr-kb-kookmin\":{\"source\":\"card.kbcard.com/CRD/DVIEW/HCAMCXPRICAC0076 (Travelers check card terms); m.kbcard.com/CRD/DVIEW/MCAMCXHIACRC0002 (ALL card); kbthink.com/card/lost.html; kbthink.com/main/living-finance/talk-cardnews/2025/lost-card.html; m.kbcard.com/SVC/DVIEW/MSFM0020; obank.kbstar.com/quics?page=C019850, read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Check card: the first three reissues in a year are free; from the fourth reissue in a year, 2,000 won each. Same rule whatever the reason.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Once a loss is reported (phone 1588-1688, KB Pay app or a branch) the card can’t be used at all; the customer can later lift the report in KB Pay if the card turns up, as long as the replacement hasn’t gone into production. Charges others made in the 60 days around the report can be partly compensated.\",\"suspectWords\":\"KB Kookmin Card runs a fraud detection system 24/7 that scores every transaction; a flagged one triggers a text message and a call from monitoring staff to confirm whether the customer made it.\"},\"kr-shinhan\":{\"source\":\"shinhancard.com/pconts/html/card/apply/check/1224650_2206.html; shinhancard.com/pconts/html/helpdesk/guide/CONFM90017/CONFM90017R01.html; shinhancard.com/pconts/html/helpdesk/guide/CONFM90017/CONFM90017R04.html; shinhancard.com/pconts/html/helpdesk/dataRoom/MOBFM164N/1199920_1119.html, auto-succession notice 2020-12-29; others read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Check card design issuance fee (1,000 won on e.g. Pick E) is charged only at first issue, not when the same design is reissued, unless the card was closed first.\",\"rushDays\":3,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Reporting a loss blocks further use of the card at once. For a customer abroad, Shinhan will send an emergency replacement card (credit cards only, no ATM or online use) to where they are staying within 1 to 3 business days depending on the card network.\"},\"kr-hana\":{\"source\":\"hanacard.co.kr/OPY35350000N.web; hanacard.co.kr/OPI95100090N.web (menu lists a card lock service); kebhana.com/cont/customer/customer05/customer0501/index.jsp, read 2026-09-26\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Reporting a loss or theft (1800-1111, 24 hours) stops the card from being used so that nobody else can charge it, and a new card can then be reissued.\"},\"kr-nh\":{\"source\":\"card.nonghyup.com/content/html/ip/ci/ipci1010c.html; card.nonghyup.com/servlet/IpCc2021R.act?CD_WRS_SQNO=90010517, read 2026-09-26\",\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer reports the loss online, at an NH NongHyup Bank branch or on 1644-4000; once a replacement is registered the old card is void immediately and stays void even if found. A fraud claim of 500,000 won or more carries a 10,000 won per-card compensation processing fee.\"},\"kr-kakaobank\":{\"source\":\"kakaobank.com/products/checkcard; brunch.co.kr/@kakaobank/71; tech.kakaobank.com/posts/2310-applying-ai-into-fds-system/, brunch post 2022-03-10; tech blog 2023-10-30; product page read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":200000,\"replaceWords\":\"2,000 won, charged only when the card is reissued because it was lost or damaged.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer can first lock domestic and overseas payments in the app, then report the loss in the app, by phone (1599-8888) or through the chatbot and order a new card; the old card is closed automatically once the new one is used, and after a reissue the loss report can only be lifted through the customer center.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When KakaoBank's fraud detection system flags a transaction, the customer is asked to verify it by video call.\"},\"au-commbank\":{\"source\":\"commbank.com.au/support/lost-stolen-or-damaged-card-support-page.html; commbank.com.au/support.credit-cards.card-delivery-time.html; commbank.com.au/support/overseas.html; SavingsInvestment_ADB2852.pdf (1 Sep 2026, s1.4.2); ADB1682.pdf credit card fees (19 Aug 2026); CommBank search snippet of support/security fraud-alert page, 1 September 2026 (account terms); 19 August 2026 (card fees); read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No fee for an ordinary replacement in Australia (none is listed in either fee schedule). A $20 emergency replacement card fee applies when an emergency card is delivered to you, typically overseas; the bank says it can send one anywhere in the world for $20.\",\"rushFee\":2000,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Reporting a card lost or stolen in the app or NetBank cancels it and orders a replacement with a new card number. You can lock a misplaced card temporarily instead, and digital wallet payments keep working while it’s locked.\",\"suspectWords\":\"An automated text arrives within seconds of possible fraud asking you to reply yes if it was you or no if it wasn't; a no brings a call from a fraud agent. App push alerts for suspicious transactions can also be turned on.\"},\"au-westpac\":{\"source\":\"westpac.com.au/personal-banking/online-banking/making-the-most/lost-stolen-card/; westpac.com.au/personal-banking/credit-cards/manage/fraud-disputes-lost-stolen-cards/replacement-after-fraud/; westpac.com.au/faq/lost-stolen-credit-card/; westpac.com.au/security/fraud-and-scams/credit-card-fraud/; PersonalAccounts-tandc.pdf (27 Aug 2026); westpac-credit-card-terms-and-conditions.pdf (27 Jun 2024, cl 3.3), 27 August 2026 (deposit terms); read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No replacement fee appears in the personal deposit account fee tables. If you are overseas you pay the courier cost; for a credit card couriered within Australia a $25 courier charge goes on the card, with more for same-day delivery.\",\"rushFee\":2500,\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"Reporting the card lost or stolen permanently cancels it (and any additional cardholder cards) and orders a replacement with a new card number. A digital card is available in the Westpac App right away, and a misplaced card can be locked for up to 15 days instead.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The Fraud Detection Team texts you to confirm the transaction and asks you to text back; if the bank can't reach you by phone it may stop the card. If fraud is confirmed it stops the card and issues new cards.\"},\"au-nab\":{\"source\":\"nab.com.au/help-support/personal-banking/manage-cards/block-replace-card; nab.com.au/personal/travel/visa-emergency-travel-assistance; personal-banking-fees-and-charges-guide.pdf (31 Oct 2025); credit-card-terms-and-conditions.pdf (18 Apr 2024); personal-transaction-savings-products-tc.pdf (cl 24.4-24.5); nab.com.au/about-us/security/report-fraud-scams; nab.com.au/news/personal-finance/blocked-card-nab-customers-can-now-unblock-it-instantly-in-the-app (17 Jun 2026), 31 October 2025 (fee guide); read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No card replacement fee is listed in the personal banking fee guide (the only card fees are Platinum Visa Debit at $10 a month and $20 to change card color). If a card is lost overseas, Visa can issue a temporary emergency card, usually within 48 to 72 hours, that expires after two months.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"A permanent block in the app or Internet Banking cancels the card and orders a replacement, which arrives in five to seven business days. You can temporarily block a misplaced card and toggle it back on if you find it, and the card keeps working in your digital wallet.\",\"suspectWords\":\"The app sends a push notification asking 'Yes, it's me' or 'No, not me', and the card may be blocked until you answer; otherwise an automated text asks you to reply 1 or 0, and a 0 brings a call from a fraud specialist. Since June 2026 customers can review flagged transactions and unblock the card in the app.\"},\"au-anz\":{\"source\":\"anz.com.au/support/online-banking/manage-your-card/lost-stolen-card/; anz.com.au/support/online-banking/manage-your-card/replace/; anz-creditcards-conditions-of-use.pdf (31 Jul 2025, cl 9.4, 19, 22); credit-card-fees-charges.pdf (25 Aug 2026); personal-account-fees-charges.pdf (1 Dec 2025); personal-banking-general-fees-charges.pdf (27 Mar 2026); anz.com.au/security/how-we-protect-you/falcon/, 25 August 2026 (card fees); read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No replacement fee in the account or credit card fee schedules. A $50 Priority Fee applies if you ask for a card or PIN to be issued and delivered as a priority, and courier delivery overseas costs $50.\",\"rushFee\":5000,\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"newNumberOnFraud\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The bank cancels the reported card and sends a replacement within 5 to 7 working days in Australia, with a new card number (a reissued card keeps its number only when it wasn't reported lost or stolen). For a credit card it may also open a new card account and move the balance across.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When its fraud system flags an unusual card transaction, ANZ may decline it or block the card and usually sends a two-way text in real time asking you to reply; once you confirm the transaction, the card should be unblocked within 15 minutes.\"},\"nz-anz\":{\"source\":\"anz.co.nz/content/dam/anzconz/documents/rates-fees-agreements/ANZ-fees-charges.pdf; anz.co.nz/content/dam/anzconz/documents/rates-fees-agreements/bank-accounts/ANZ-EFTPOS-card-and-ANZ-visa-debit-card-conditions-of-use.pdf; anz.co.nz/personal/credit-cards/manage/lost-stolen/; anz.co.nz/banking-with-anz/ways-to-bank/guides/cards/; anz.co.nz/banking-with-anz/banking-safely/fraud-protection/fraud-check/, Fees and Charges effective 1 September 2026; debit card Conditions of Use effective 13 April 2026; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":500,\"replaceFeeCredit\":500,\"replaceWords\":\"$5 per card for EFTPOS, Visa Debit and credit cards, lost and stolen included; urgent delivery is charged at the actual courier fee, in New Zealand or overseas. A lost card isn’t replaced while the customer is overseas; ANZ waits until they are back in New Zealand. No charge for the replacement wallet card in Apple Pay or Google Pay.\",\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The card is canceled in goMoney, Internet Banking or by phone and stops working for new transactions (ATM withdrawals can take up to 15 minutes to block), direct debits set up on the Visa Debit number stop, and the Apple Pay or Google Pay wallet card is canceled and re-created automatically for the replacement. The replacement is ordered at the customer's request and mailed out.\",\"suspectWords\":\"ANZ Fraud Check sends a text or email about the unusual transaction and the customer replies Yes or No; the card may be blocked until they reply, stays blocked if ANZ can't reach them, and a No reply cancels the card and a replacement may be ordered.\"},\"nz-asb\":{\"source\":\"asb.co.nz/how-to/how-to-cancel-and-replace-your-asb-card.html (Wayback 2026-05-13); asb.co.nz/help/my-credit-card-has-been-stolen--or-ive-lost-it--what-should-i-do.html (Wayback 2026-06-15); asb.co.nz/banking-with-asb/card-control-faq.html (Wayback 2026-06-11); asb.co.nz/help/why-would-my-visa-credit-card-or-visa-debit-card-not-work-when-trying-to-shop-online.html (Wayback 2026-03-12); asb.co.nz/content/dam/asb/documents/banking-with-asb/2024/asb-banking-with-asb-guide-to-fees-01-july-2024.pdf (Wayback), Guide to fees 1 July 2024 (the 15 June 2026 guide was blocked); help pages as archived March to June 2026; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No replacement card fee is listed for Visa Debit or credit cards; only overseas card delivery is charged ('applicable courier service fee'). Standard delivery is 5 to 7 business days in New Zealand; overseas delivery depends on local carriers.\",\"standardDays\":7,\"lockInApp\":true,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer cancels and replaces the card in the ASB app (Cards & devices), FastNet Classic, by phone or in a branch; the old card is canceled immediately and the new one is mailed within 5 to 7 business days. Apple Pay and Google Pay keep working and switch to the new card details around 5 a.m. the next day.\",\"suspectWords\":\"ASB's fraud monitoring may block a transaction, and ASB then contacts the customer to confirm whether they made it, by card security alert, phone call, email or text message.\"},\"nz-bnz\":{\"source\":\"bnz.co.nz/support/mobile-banking/cards/cancelling-and-replacing-your-card; bnz.co.nz/personal-banking/everyday-banking/everyday-cards; bnz.co.nz/support/mobile-banking/cards/blocking-and-unblocking-your-card; bnz.co.nz/assets/about-us/terms-conditions/pdfs/bnz-credit-card-terms-conditions.pdf; bnz.co.nz/support/credit-cards/security/unusual-transactions, Credit card Terms and Conditions 7 May 2025; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"No fee when a card is replaced because it’s faulty, damaged, lost or stolen; if the customer chooses courier delivery, a courier charge may apply (amount not published).\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer calls BNZ or cancels the card in the app and orders a replacement, which arrives within 10 business days; the old card must be cut up if it turns up. The replacement arrives unblocked but has to be activated.\",\"suspectWords\":\"BNZ's transaction monitoring may decline suspicious transactions or block the card for security; the pages read don’t say whether BNZ texts or calls, and they tell the customer to call 0800 735 901 if they suspect fraud.\"},\"nz-westpac\":{\"source\":\"westpac.co.nz/assets/About-us/legal-information-privacy/documents/Transaction-and-service-fees-Personal-Banking-Westpac-NZ.pdf; westpac.co.nz/help/how-to-block-or-cancel-and-replace-a-lost-stolen-or-damaged-credit-or-debit-card/ (Wayback 2026-09-03); westpac.co.nz/help/i-do-not-wish-for-my-credit-or-debit-card-to-be-opted-into-automatic-billing-updater/; westpac.co.nz/credit-cards/managing-your-credit-card/card-security-tips/; assets.dam.westpac.co.nz Debit Mastercard and Fee Free Mastercard Conditions of Use, Transaction and service fees effective 31 July 2026; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":1000,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"Debit Mastercard and EFTPOS replacements cost $10 plus courier costs where applicable; credit card replacements cost $0 plus courier costs where applicable. Standard delivery is 5 to 10 days. An expiring credit card is reissued free the month before expiry.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"The customer cancels the card in Westpac One or at a branch and Westpac permanently blocks the old card; the new card should arrive in 5 to 10 days, and Apple Pay or Google Pay keep working meanwhile. Mastercard's Automatic Billing Updater doesn’t apply to a card replaced because it was lost, stolen or used fraudulently, so the customer updates recurring payments themselves.\",\"suspectWords\":\"When a transaction looks unusual, Westpac tries to reach the customer by phone (8 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. local time), email or text first; if it can't, it may put a temporary block on the card, lifted at once if the customer confirms the spending is genuine, and a confirmed fraud gets the card fully blocked and replaced.\"},\"nz-kiwibank\":{\"source\":\"kiwibank.co.nz/help/cards/order-or-cancel/replace/; kiwibank.co.nz/help/cards/lost-or-stolen-card/; kiwibank.co.nz/help/fraud-scams/how-we-protect-you/; media.kiwibank.co.nz/media/documents/Personal_Banking_Fees_and_Limits_May26.pdf, Personal Banking Fees and Limits effective 14 May 2026; read 2026-09-26\",\"replaceFeeDebit\":0,\"replaceFeeCredit\":0,\"replaceWords\":\"The current fees guide (effective 14 May 2026) lists no card replacement or card courier fee for Visa Debit, EFTPOS or credit cards. Lost, stolen or damaged Visa Debit and credit cards can be replaced; EFTPOS cards only if lost or stolen.\",\"standardDays\":10,\"lockInApp\":true,\"updaterToBills\":false,\"lostCardWords\":\"Ordering a replacement in the app cancels the old card at once and a new one is mailed, arriving within 10 business days; Apple Pay and Google Pay keep working. If the new card has a different number, the customer has to update their regular payments and saved card details themselves.\",\"suspectWords\":\"If Kiwibank notices unusual spending it may send a text or email asking whether the customer made the transaction; if it can't reach them and fraud looks likely, it may temporarily block the card until they speak.\"}}");

